  "worked_solution": "First, because the initial condition is $y(0)=2,$ we fill $y=2$ into the table.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{\u2032}\\,$ | $\\,\u0394y\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $2$ | $$ | $$ |\n\nNext, we compute ${y}^{\u2032}$ according to the given rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{\u2032} & =\\sqrt{0+{2}^{2}-3} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1} \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we add this to our table.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{\u2032}\\,$ | $\\,\u0394y\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $2$ | $1$ | $$ |\n\nFinally, we compute $\u0394y$ using Euler's method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\u0394y & ={y}^{\u2032}\\cdot \u0394x \\\\  & =1(\\frac{1}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe add this to our table.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{\u2032}\\,$ | $\\,\u0394y\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $2$ | $1$ | $\\frac{1}{3}$ |",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
